# Variables & Environment
# File-level @variables must appear BEFORE the first ### request separator
# so httpyac treats them as file-scoped (not tied to an empty request block).
#
# Nested: @baseUrl = https://{{host}} is supported by httpyac.

@host = httpbin.org
@baseUrl = https://{{host}}
@contentType = application/json
@protocol = https
@domain = api.example.com
@apiBase = {{protocol}}://{{domain}}
@version = v2
@endpoint = {{apiBase}}/{{version}}
@token = my-secret-bearer-token
@userId = 42

### GET using variables
GET {{baseUrl}}/get
Accept: {{contentType}}

### POST using variables in URL, headers, and body
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "server": "{{host}}",
  "message": "sent from Zed HTTPyac Client"
}

### Deeply nested variable
# Resolves to: https://api.example.com/v2/users
GET {{endpoint}}/users
Accept: application/json

### Variable in URL path
GET {{baseUrl}}/anything/users/{{userId}}

### Variable in header value
GET {{baseUrl}}/headers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Variable in request body
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "token": "{{token}}"
}

### Using environment variable (requires http-client.env.json + activeEnv)
# Uncomment after setting activeEnv / Switch Environment:
# GET {{api_url}}/get
# Authorization: Bearer {{api_key}}
